<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="wet-burr" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Burritos - Wet</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Filling:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 pound ground beef</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup chopped onion</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 clove garlic, minced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>2 teaspoons chili powder</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon dried oregano</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon ground cumin</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> teaspoon pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>15 ounces black beans</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Sauce:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 tablespoons butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{3}{4}</m> cup water</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>8 ounces tomato sauce</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoons chili powder</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Boullion cube</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{3}{4}</m> teaspoon cumin</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a large skillet cook ground beef, onion, and garlic.  Drain well.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add chili powder, oregano, cumin, salt, and pepper; simmer for 5 minutes. Add beans and <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup of the sauce (see below). Cook until heated through; keep warm.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          For sauce, melt the butter and stir in the flour until smooth.  Stir in the water and bring to a boil until the sauce thickens.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add tomato sauce, chili powder, boullion, and cumin.  Simmer for 5 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Wrap tortillas in foil; bake at <m>350^\circ</m> for 10 minutes, or until thoroughly heated. Spoon about <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup ground beef mixture on each warm tortilla. Roll tightly and place seam-side down on plate. When all burritos are made, spoon remaining sauce over the burritos.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>